<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaranj</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zarang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaranj is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, capital of Nimruz province, on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. As the chief town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> in the early Islamic centuries, it was the base from which the Saffarid ruler Ya'qub ibn al-Layth rose to power in 861, and later the seat of the Nasrid and Mihrabanid maliks. The medieval city was sacked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> in 1383.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaranj.jpg" alt="Zaranj" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sgt. Mallory S. VanderSchans, U.S. Marine Corps · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afghanistan-Iran_border_in_Zaranj,_Afghanistan,_2011.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
